            "review_text": "RRGT\nBatangas City, Philippines251 contributions\n0\nClose Enough\nApr 2022 • Solo\nMy family and I always go to Coco Ichibanya for our Japanese Curry fix whether in our home country or when visiting Japan. It was a pleasant surprise to find it in HCMC. Whereas in Japan, it is more typical for the outlets to be small, hole in the wall type places with bar seating and a few booths and tables, this was a well and proper restaurant. Ordered the pork cutlet omelette curry and it was close enough to what I expect. The cutlet was thinner than what is typical in Japan but the star is the curry after all and that was delicious as always and coated the fluffy Japanese rice. The local crew spoke English so no issues with ordering and service. One difference I noted is that drinking water is always served to guests in Japan but I had to make do with soda in this case. No big deal. I hope to be back soon here in HCMC for this.\nRead more\nWritten April 11, 2022",
